Subject: [PATCH] restyle small-ruminants module to the dark system theme
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The whole module (Flock, Health, Breeding, Weights, Milk, Sales, plus the
financial/breeding/performance analytics pages) was still on the original
light Tailwind palette (bg-slate-50/bg-white/text-slate-*) while Dairy,
Poultry, and Coffee had all moved to the dark obsidian palette
(bg-[#0A0C10]/bg-[#0D0F14]/border-[#2A2D35] etc — see globals.css, which
already called this module out by name as a known gap). Brings every
small-ruminants page onto the same tokens: page bg, card bg, borders,
text hierarchy (white/#D1D5DB/#9CA3AF/#6B7280/#4B5563), and the
bg-*-950/50 + text-*-300 badge convention used elsewhere for status
chips (payment status, sale type, event type, pregnancy status, etc).

Also, while restyling each page:
- Dropped the per-page duplicate 'SubNav'/back-arrow headers
  (SalesClient, BreedingClient, MilkClient, WeightsClient, HealthClient,
  and the three analytics pages all rolled their own copy of the
  Flock/Health/Breeding/Weights/Milk/Sales tab strip, or a redundant
  back-arrow). EnterpriseNavHeader (rendered by DashboardShell) already
  puts these tabs above every route in the module, so each page now just
  has its own title strip + page actions, matching the pattern already
  used by SmallRuminantsClient.tsx and the dairy/poultry/coffee finance
  pages.
- Fixed AnimalCard.tsx reading animal.date_of_birth for age, when every
  caller (SmallRuminantsClient, etc.) passes birth_date — every animal
  card showed 'Unknown age' regardless of actual birth date. Now checks
  both field names.
